  "ownsLevel": {
    "confidence": "verified",
    "items": [
      "The `ccBGSSSE025_` records are in `ccbgssse025-advdsgs.esm`. The summoned Ash Spawn and Ash Guardians are on *Undead Summons*. The AtrForge copies (`ccBGSSSE025_EncSummon{GoldenSaint,DarkSeducer}{Archer,Warrior}AtrForge` 1CAD42–1CAD45) are the hostile saints the pack's quest spawns, so they are on *Golden Saints & Dark Seducers*.",
      "The Golden Saint and Dark Seducer summons (`…Archer` 095E1F, `…Warrior` 095E20, `…DarkSeducerArcher` 095E21, `…DarkSeducerWarrior` 095E22, level 18; Thoron's `…Boss` 0BE6B2–0BE6B5, PC ×0.75 [18–80]) use the base saints `ccBGSSSE025_Enc{GoldenSaint,DarkSeducer}{Archer,Warrior}` 000880 · 0009C8 · 000A06 · 000A07 (on *Golden Saints & Dark Seducers*) as their template but not for `Stats`: changing a base saint leaves every summon at its own level.",
      "`ccBGSSSE025_EncSummonStaada` 19D3FD uses `ccBGSSSE025_Staada` 198273 (on *Golden Saints & Dark Seducers*) as its template but not for `Stats`, and `…StaadaHostile` 1B1815 templates 19D3FD the same way: all three keep level 42 separately.",
      "The other summons follow the placed creature through `Stats`: `DLC2SummonSeeker` from `DLC2EncSeeker01` 028E7F:Dragonborn.esm and `DLC2SummonSeekerHigh` from `DLC2EncSeeker03` 028E83:Dragonborn.esm (on *Seeker*), `ccPEWSSE002_SummonLurker` from `DLC2EncLurker01` 01B640:Dragonborn.esm (on *Lurker*), `DLC1EncGargoyleSummon` from `DLC1EncGargoyleSmall` 017702:Dawnguard.esm (on *Gargoyle*); changing those changes the summons.",
      "`ccPEWSSE002_SummonSeeker` 00084E:ccpewsse002-armsofchaos.esl (named \"Lurker\", `Stats` from `DLC2EncSeeker01`) is in neither Sovereign Band list and no effect names it: the lists draw the Dragonborn `DLC2SummonSeeker` instead.",
      "Every row: no other record keeps its own level.",
      "Every other record (`DLC1dunHarkonEncGargoyleSummon`, the `ccBGSSSE025_LvlSummon*AtrForge` wrappers) carries `Stats` and follows its template or list."
    ]
  },
